, Louisiana.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Gerry Janelle Frost | President, CEO, Principal Accounting & Financial Officer and Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["AMERISAFE, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $363M market cap on $317M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 16-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $9M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.23\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 13.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 81% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8147023794694217},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 48% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"AMERISAFE (AMSF) \u2013 Research Analysts\u2019 Recent Ratings Changes","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/amerisafe-amsf-research-analysts-recent-ratings-changes.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793663815.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.052,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"AMERISAFE (NASDAQ:AMSF) Stock Price Target Lowered at Truist Financial","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/31/amerisafe-nasdaqamsf-stock-price-target-lowered-at-truist-financial.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793437393.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Responsive Playbooks and the AMSF Inflection","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/34/Responsive_Playbooks_and_th